# ASF Cursor Rules

- Start from `AGENTS.md` and the active `tasks/EPIC-*.md`.
- Treat `docs/` and `decisions/` as source of truth. Do not contradict Accepted ADRs.
- Use project skill `.cursor/skills/asf-mvp` when implementing MVP work.
- MVP stack: FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Telegram, Whisper STT. No Redis, no Neo4j, no microservices.
- Keep modular monolith package boundaries (`apps`, `core`, `knowledge`, `discovery`, `integrations`). Owner TZ console lives in `apps/console` + `/console/api` (DEC-007).
- Prefer stubs/interfaces for LLM and STT; inject real providers via settings.
- Do not invent scope beyond product types: website, telegram_bot, rest_service, ai_automation.
- Raise human review instead of guessing on blocking product decisions.
- New platform features must pass the MVP filter or go to `backlog/Future.md`.
- Write tests for new behavior; keep handlers thin.
